# Godot's per-capture stdout (~31KB each, almost entirely engine boot noise) and the
# intermediate captures the controls produce on every run. The captures worth keeping as a
# record are committed explicitly; these regenerate in one command.
*.log
det_run*.png
# Control 5's RED runs write no PNG at all — that is the point. Listed so nobody adds one.
junction_lit_red_*.png
scene_normal.png
scene_floor_is_wall.png
probe/arm_*.png

# ...except the device boot log, which is the ONLY artefact proving the corridor renders on the
# reference device rather than merely being installed there. Pulled off the phone with
# `devicectl device copy from --domain-type appDataContainer`.
!DEVICE-boot-diag.log
